When a new user is created, there are two attributes in Keycloak that should be set and exposed via a JWT token to enable data segregation per role:

Organization ID: Also referred to as tenant_id. Keycloak does not provide this attribute out of the box. You need to add it as a custom attribute and configure a Protocol Mapper to inject it into the JWT as a claim. In this case, the RBAC middleware should generate the organization ID (UUID v4) and send it to Keycloak when creating the user.

User ID: Keycloak automatically generates the user ID (sub) when creating the user.

Keycloak provides an Admin API, which allows you to create new users, set temporary passwords, and assign roles. To use this API, you need a preconfigured service account with a client ID and secret in Keycloak. These credentials are required to invoke the Admin API endpoints.